deo another important component  is ketchup which can be used for  automated hyper parameter tuning hyper  parameter tuning plays a major part in  developing good models and manually  searching a hyper parameter space can  take a lot of effort cat dev helps you  optimize your hyper parameter values  around a metric you've chosen such as  the accuracy of the model it's a helpful  way to find and visualize the optimum  configuration to prepare your model for  production next up Q flow pipelines is a  powerful platform to help you build and  m/l workflows pipelines lets you build a  set of steps to handle everything from  collecting data to serving your model  it's based on containers so each step is  portable and scalable you can run your  same pipelines code across environments  and share it with others and since each  step is independent you can reuse  pipeline steps for different pipelines  and experiments chances are you're  probably gonna want to strain your model  cube flow supports several ML frameworks  for training such as sensor flow and  pipe torch cube flow defines custom  kubernetes resources for distributed  training jobs so you can create a config  file that specifies the details you want  to use for training and let it handle  the rest you have the flexibility to  choose the tools you want to use or  you're already using to train and  retrain your model we'll walk through  some training in future videos of course  your models may not be too useful unless  you can actually make predictions with  them you Flo can serve your models with  multiple frameworks like TF serving KF  serving and Selden Corps you could even  plug in your own serving system if  needed but KF serving can help abstract  most common ml frameworks it's built on  K native a framework for running  serverless apps on kubernetes that way  you can serve your model and access all  the resources you need without having to  handle the complexities directly this is  just a brief overview of the major  components in cube flow there's lots of  examples you can try out for yourself  but we'll also go deeper and talk more  about each of these in upcoming videos  check out the link below to try it out  for yourself and stay tuned  [Music]  [Applause]
 

